1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:03,440
As a child already, I kept documents and postcards.

2
00:00:03,970 --> 00:00:06,540
And then of course, as you grow up, your mind opens.

3
00:00:07,730 --> 00:00:08,620
At that time, I was living in Toulouse.

4
00:00:09,500 --> 00:00:12,280
I used to go to flea markets, and naturally I came across postcards of Montricoux.

5
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:14,140
I was moved to see my village.

6
00:00:15,280 --> 00:00:17,980
Then I bought paintings from nearby villages,

7
00:00:18,140 --> 00:00:21,060
Bruniquel, Penne, all those beautiful villages of the Aveyron valley.

8
00:00:22,240 --> 00:00:24,440
And then I came across drawings and paintings.

9
00:00:25,340 --> 00:00:27,820
Little by little, I built up this collection.

10
00:00:28,520 --> 00:00:29,260
Can we go upstairs and take a look?

11
00:00:29,460 --> 00:00:30,440
Of course, with pleasure.

12
00:00:31,680 --> 00:00:33,920
I don’t have enough room to display everything, there are artworks everywhere.

13
00:00:36,240 --> 00:00:37,060
You see, they are everywhere.

14
00:00:37,820 --> 00:00:39,300
It is filled with Marcel-Lenoir works.

15
00:00:40,620 --> 00:00:41,480
Here too, they are everywhere.

16
00:00:42,240 --> 00:00:42,920
I also have them at home.

17
00:00:43,920 --> 00:00:44,580
All of this is completely filled.

18
00:00:44,930 --> 00:00:48,120
It took me years to acquire all of this.

19
00:00:49,240 --> 00:00:52,820
And then one day you told yourself, “I can’t just leave all this piled up in my garage.”

20
00:00:54,460 --> 00:00:57,760
I try to make all these artists known.

21
00:00:58,540 --> 00:01:00,280
With the goal of creating a museum?

22
00:01:00,920 --> 00:01:01,660
Yes, eventually, yes.

23
00:01:02,540 --> 00:01:03,260
I am going to create a museum.

24
00:01:03,710 --> 00:01:04,300
I will show it to you.

25
00:01:12,100 --> 00:01:13,140
I don’t know if there is a photograph.

26
00:01:19,080 --> 00:01:20,680
You can see the condition the house was in.

27
00:01:21,220 --> 00:01:23,020
I should have taken many more photographs.

28
00:01:23,160 --> 00:01:24,060
You can see how the entrance looked.

29
00:01:25,000 --> 00:01:26,020
It used to be a window.

30
00:01:27,780 --> 00:01:29,760
There, I rebuilt everything myself at the back.

31
00:01:31,390 --> 00:01:31,480
Everything.

32
00:01:31,780 --> 00:01:33,320
But when? When were you doing all this?

33
00:01:33,480 --> 00:01:35,260
I did this every weekend.

34
00:01:36,700 --> 00:01:39,400
I started the restoration work in 1993.

35
00:01:39,920 --> 00:01:41,560
It took me five years to restore it.

36
00:01:41,770 --> 00:01:42,700
I worked every weekend.

37
00:01:43,260 --> 00:01:44,140
I rebuilt everything at the back.

38
00:01:44,760 --> 00:01:46,040
It had all collapsed into the neighbor’s property.

39
00:01:46,480 --> 00:01:48,440
And afterward, there was a pillar here.

40
00:01:49,980 --> 00:01:50,840
A large pillar.

41
00:01:51,230 --> 00:01:52,180
Everything was mixed together.

42
00:01:52,800 --> 00:01:54,700
There was earth and timber everywhere.

43
00:01:55,400 --> 00:01:56,820
Then I reinforced everything.

44
00:01:57,340 --> 00:01:58,700
I asw the one who added de beam.

45
00:01:58,720 --> 00:02:00,180
That one wasn't there, you see, it's a recent addition.

46
00:02:00,600 --> 00:02:02,480
That is the original part. I reinforced everything,

47
00:02:02,620 --> 00:02:04,360
and below as well. And I worked like that throughout.

48
00:02:05,540 --> 00:02:06,540
I began building

49
00:02:06,620 --> 00:02:08,119
the staircase, the wooden floor,

50
00:02:09,300 --> 00:02:10,780
the fireplace, I built that too.

51
00:02:11,219 --> 00:02:12,220
I put it as a decoration.

52
00:02:13,000 --> 00:02:13,360
Yes, yes.

53
00:02:14,859 --> 00:02:15,180
That's no small feat!
